# Repo-root .dockerignore — read ONLY by builds whose CONTEXT IS THE REPO ROOT
# (the ddl-apply + eod-controller images, context: ../../..). The ingestion/
# compute/gateway/bridge builds use context code/ and read code/.dockerignore
# instead — keep the two files in sync (P5-015). Keeps the context lean: git,
# build output, and logs. The schema-compat matrix evidence is gitignored
# (R-051) and RUNTIME-ONLY per ddl-apply/Dockerfile ("no image COPY is
# needed") — nothing under logs/ is re-included (P5-003/004).
.git
.freebuff
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*_rsa
**/*_dsa
**/credentials*
**/secrets/
**/target
**/node_modules
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.idea/
**/.vscode/
**/*.iml
**/.DS_Store
**/*.log
**/logs/
# Host-local, git-ignored build outputs (Go binaries in go-bridge/) and
# Eclipse/JDT metadata: neither is a build input for any image, and both churn
# or grow the context for no benefit. Keep in sync with code/.dockerignore
# (P5-015) and with the stamp inputs — image_staleness_check.py now treats the
# context's .dockerignore as an image input, so editing this file relabels.
**/arrow-bridge
**/faketool/faketool
**/.classpath
**/.project
**/.factorypath
**/.settings/
**/dependency-reduced-pom.xml
